From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:12:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ccGLWindowStereo: give the window its stereo format

The stereo window kept its QSurfaceFormat (stereo, double buffer) for the OpenGL context but never set it on the QWindow, so Qt
chose a visual without GLX_STEREO and isQuadBufferSupported() answered no.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libs/qCC_glWindow/src/ccGLWindowStereo.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/qCC_glWindow/src/ccGLWindowStereo.cpp b/libs/qCC_glWindow/src/ccGLWindowStereo.cpp
index 46f8c9b..efd194c 100644
--- a/libs/qCC_glWindow/src/ccGLWindowStereo.cpp
+++ b/libs/qCC_glWindow/src/ccGLWindowStereo.cpp
@@ -47,6 +47,10 @@ ccGLWindowStereo::ccGLWindowStereo(	QSurfaceFormat* format/*=nullptr*/,
 
 	m_format = format ? *format : requestedFormat();
 
+	// Qt picks the native window's visual from the window's own format: without this the window gets no stereo visual
+	// (GLX_STEREO) and quad-buffered stereo reports "not supported" although the context asks for it
+	setFormat(m_format);
+
 	//default picking mode
 	setPickingMode(DEFAULT_PICKING);
 
